# Not formatted at all.
#
# These are verbatim transcriptions of the original implementations the ported
# SIMD routines are checked against, kept beside the .asm they came from. Being
# readable as a copy of that assembly and of the 2005 C++ is their whole purpose,
# so they are left as transcribed and diffable against their source rather than
# restyled. Reformatting them would be behaviour-preserving but would cost the
# one property they exist to have.
#
# DisableFormat makes clang-format return the input unchanged, so the hook and
# the CI check both pass over these files without special-casing them. The
# explicit SortIncludes is needed with it: DisableFormat alone does not stop
# include sorting.
DisableFormat: true
SortIncludes: Never
